Subject: [PATCH] stamp-p4: PR_SET_SYSTEM_WORK task mark + reserve-gate override (#51 round 4)

0090's ancestry test marks console/SSH-launched work "user", which also
catches system scripts a user happens to start: `S40network restart` from
the console or an SSH session marks the whole restart subtree (udhcpc,
ifconfig, route, default.script) user, so the reserve gate throttles
system maintenance work and denied allocations that buddy cannot serve
become real ENOMEMs (measured: 51/21 on the reserve arms).

PR_SET_SYSTEM_WORK gives such scripts an explicit override: set once by
root via prctl(), the per-task flag wins over the ctty/ancestor test and
-- because it lives in task_struct->flags -- it survives exec and is
inherited by fork (copy_flags() only strips
PF_SUPERPRIV|PF_WQ_WORKER|PF_IDLE|PF_NO_SETAFFINITY).  A tiny
`run-system CMD...` wrapper does prctl+exec, so shell scripts opt in
with a one-line re-exec at the top.

arg2=1 marks, arg2=0 clears the mark (the task then classifies by
ancestry again) -- both directions are allowed so a wrapped helper can
still run user-side children if it ever needs to; clearing never
escalates anything since the mark only widens pool access for the task
that has it.  CAP_SYS_ADMIN is required, so only root can move itself
out of the user class.

The flag is also visible in /proc/<pid>/stat field 9 (flags), so the
measurement harness attributes flag-marked processes to the system side
without name lists.

Applies on top of 0090 (the classification hunk targets
nommu_task_is_user).  Staged only with NOMMU_USER_RESERVE=1 and
NOMMU_SYSTEM_MARK=1; kernels built without it return EINVAL from
the prctl and run-system execs the target anyway, so the wrapped
scripts keep working unchanged.
---
diff --git a/include/linux/sched.h b/include/linux/sched.h
--- a/include/linux/sched.h
+++ b/include/linux/sched.h
@@ -1815,5 +1815,5 @@
 #define PF_BLOCK_TS		0x20000000	/* plug has ts that needs updating */
-#define PF__HOLE__40000000	0x40000000
+#define PF_SYSTEM_WORK	0x40000000	/* #51: ancestry overrides to the system side of the pool gate */
 #define PF_SUSPEND_TASK		0x80000000      /* This thread called freeze_processes() and should not be frozen */
 
 /*
diff --git a/include/uapi/linux/prctl.h b/include/uapi/linux/prctl.h
--- a/include/uapi/linux/prctl.h
+++ b/include/uapi/linux/prctl.h
@@ -415,4 +415,7 @@
 # define PR_CFI_DISABLE		_BITUL(1)
 # define PR_CFI_LOCK		_BITUL(2)
 
+/* #51: mark/unmark the calling task as system for the NOMMU user pool */
+#define PR_SET_SYSTEM_WORK	0x45535459	/* 'ESTY' */
+
 #endif /* _LINUX_PRCTL_H */
diff --git a/kernel/sys.c b/kernel/sys.c
--- a/kernel/sys.c
+++ b/kernel/sys.c
@@ -2907,6 +2907,17 @@
 		if (arg3 & PR_CFI_LOCK && !(arg3 & PR_CFI_DISABLE))
 			error = arch_prctl_lock_branch_landing_pad_state(me);
 		break;
+	case PR_SET_SYSTEM_WORK:
+		if (arg3 || arg4 || arg5)
+			return -EINVAL;
+		/* Only root may move a task across the pool-gate boundary. */
+		if (!capable(CAP_SYS_ADMIN))
+			return -EPERM;
+		if (arg2)
+			me->flags |= PF_SYSTEM_WORK;
+		else
+			me->flags &= ~PF_SYSTEM_WORK;
+		break;
 	default:
 		trace_task_prctl_unknown(option, arg2, arg3, arg4, arg5);
 		error = -EINVAL;
diff --git a/mm/nommu_userspace_pool.c b/mm/nommu_userspace_pool.c
--- a/mm/nommu_userspace_pool.c
+++ b/mm/nommu_userspace_pool.c
@@ -81,6 +81,13 @@
  * itself, * helpers, the boot sync) sit outside both trees
  * and stay unmarked.  The PF_KTHREAD guard also keeps get_current_tty
  * away from sighand-less kernel threads.
+ *
+ * PF_SYSTEM_WORK wins over both tests: scripts that spawn system
+ * work (S40network & friends, started by a user on the console or over
+ * SSH) drop the inherited user mark via prctl(PR_SET_SYSTEM_WORK)
+ * before forking children, so a user-requested restart cannot drain
+ * the reserve and its transient helpers cannot be denied into real
+ * ENOMEMs.  The flag survives exec and inherits through fork.
  */
 static bool nommu_task_is_user(void)
 {
@@ -91,6 +98,9 @@
 	if (current->flags & PF_KTHREAD)
 		return false;
 
+	if (current->flags & PF_SYSTEM_WORK)
+		return false;
+
 	tty = get_current_tty();
 	if (tty) {
 		bool on_console = !strcmp(tty->name, "ttyGS1");
